<title>UK: London tea auction sees selective demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees selective demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Tea Auction saw selective demand with Assams and most bright liquoring East Africans losing two-to-five pence per kg, the official report said on Monday.</p>
<p>Some best East Africans held values while coloury mediums were steady to three pence easier.</p>
<p>Offshore teas saw fair demand at firm rates, the report said.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
